  "text": "__)\n\n\nTo solve the problem, we need to find all integer bases \\( b > 9 \\) for which \\( 17_b \\) is a divisor of \\( 97_b \\).\n\n### Step 1: Convert the numbers from base \\( b \\) to base 10\nFirst, we convert \\( 17_b \\) and \\( 97_b \\) to base 10.\n\n- \\( 17_b = 1 \\cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \\)\n- \\( 97_b = 9 \\cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \\)\n\n### Step 2: Set up the divisibility condition\nWe need \\( b + 7 \\) to divide \\( 9b + 7 \\). This means there exists an integer \\( k \\) such that:\n\n\\[\n9b + 7 = k(b + 7)\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Solve for \\( k \\)\nRearrange the equation to solve for \\( k \\):\n\n\\[\n9b + 7 = k(b + 7)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9b + 7 = kb + 7k\n\\]\n\n\\[\n9b - kb = 7k - 7\n\\]\n\n\\[\nb(9 - k) = 7(k - 1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Find integer solutions for \\( b \\)\nWe need \\( b \\) to be an integer greater than 9. Let's analyze the equation:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k}\n\\]\n\nFor \\( b \\) to be an integer, \\( 9 - k \\) must divide \\( 7(k - 1) \\). Let's find the possible values of \\( k \\) such that \\( b > 9 \\).\n\n#### Case 1: \\( k = 8 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \\frac{49}{1} = 49\n\\]\nCheck if \\( 49 > 9 \\): Yes.\n\n#### Case 2: \\( k = 7 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(7 - 1)}{9 - 7} = \\frac{42}{2} = 21\n\\]\nCheck if \\( 21 > 9 \\): Yes.\n\n#### Case 3: \\( k = 6 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(6 - 1)}{9 - 6} = \\frac{35}{3} \\approx 11.666\n\\]\nNot an integer.\n\n#### Case 4: \\( k = 5 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(5 - 1)}{9 - 5} = \\frac{28}{4} = 7\n\\]\nCheck if \\( 7 > 9 \\): No.\n\n#### Case 5: \\( k = 4 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(4 - 1)}{9 - 4} = \\frac{21}{5} = 4.2\n\\]\nNot an integer.\n\n#### Case 6: \\( k = 3 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(3 - 1)}{9 - 3} = \\frac{14}{6} \\approx 2.333\n\\]\nNot an integer.\n\n#### Case 7: \\( k = 2 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(2 - 1)}{9 - 2} = \\frac{7}{7} = 1\n\\]\nCheck if \\( 1 > 9 \\): No.\n\n#### Case 8: \\( k = 1 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(1 - 1)}{9 - 1} = 0\n\\]\nCheck if \\( 0 > 9 \\): No.\n\n#### Case 9: \\( k = 0 \\)\n\\[\nb = \\frac{7(0 - 1)}{9 - 0} = \\frac{-7}{9} \\approx -0.777\n\\]\nNot an integer.\n\n### Step 5: Sum the valid bases\nThe valid bases are \\( b = 49 \\) and \\( b = 21 \\). Sum them:\n\n\\[\n49 + 21 = 70\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]",
